  "narrative": "All estimates are signed to the registered hypothesis direction, so positive signed values support the claimed direction. I accepted claims when the signed estimate and the signed interval bound nearest zero both exceeded 0.15 composite dependency-score units; rejected claims when the favorable interval bound fell well below the threshold or the estimate was clearly opposite; and left borderline results unresolved when the interval still contained threshold-sized favorable effects but the evidence did not support acceptance. For pre-specified follow-up contexts that failed to clear threshold, I often closed further investigation even without a strict rejection, to avoid continuing arbitrary subgroup mining. PTEN loss remains the central borderline case. H107, PTEN loss among TP53-loss-free and KEAP1-loss-free cells, gives +0.255 with lower bound +0.165 and exposed n=164; I accept it as a discovery-supported conditional association and keep it active. H108, PTEN loss among TP53-loss-free and SMARCA4-loss-free cells, gives +0.261 with lower bound +0.172 and exposed n=165; I accept it but defer it because it is highly overlapping with H80, H95, H94, and H107. Together these support a reproducible context-specific PTEN-loss pattern in supplied data, but not a general main-effect association. I request validation for H80, PTEN loss among TP53-loss-free cells, because it is the broadest pre-specified PTEN context and has the largest exposed discovery cell, n=212, with lower bound +0.169. If validation clears threshold, PTEN can be promoted to a robust conditional association in the supplied dataset; if it does not, PTEN should remain reported as near-threshold and context-limited. CDKN2A context test H109 gives +0.125 with lower +0.051. The point estimate and lower bound fail the threshold, so I close follow-up, while leaving status unresolved because the interval still reaches +0.199 and thus does not strictly exclude a threshold-sized effect. The driver screens mostly close: BRAF V600E H57 and ERBB2 amplification H59 have upper favorable bounds only +0.071 and +0.094, respectively, so reject and close. EGFR amplification H58 is positive +0.092 with upper +0.197, too uncertain for acceptance but too wide for rejection, so unresolved and deferred. The MSI-high result is decisive but directionally opposite to H60: H60 is rejected because the signed positive-direction interval is strongly negative. The opposite claim H106 is signed +0.792 with lower +0.676 and exposed n=130; I accept and activate H106 as a new strong supplied-dataset association, meaning MSI-high samples have more negative composite dependency scores than MSI-high-free samples. I request validation for PTEN H80 now rather than MSI-high because MSI-high has a large effect and relatively tight interval, whereas PTEN is the borderline conclusion needing independent resolution. Constructed signature_c results show robust TP53-loss and KEAP1-loss effects in both halves: TP53 H110 +0.391 lower +0.262 and H111 +0.455 lower +0.310; KEAP1 H112 +0.816 lower +0.722 and H113 +0.849 lower +0.756. I accept and close these as heterogeneity characterization only, without biological mechanism claims. The KEAP1-by-hypoxia interaction H114 is opposite to the claimed direction and has upper favorable bound +0.119, below threshold, so reject and close. Overall, the strongest supplied-dataset associations remain TP53-loss positive/less-negative, KEAP1-loss positive/less-negative, and SMARCA4-loss negative/more-negative; MSI-high negative/stronger-dependency is newly supported. PTEN remains context-specific and borderline pending validation. These are observational associations in the supplied dataset, not causal or generalizable biological claims.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 7 appraise update: New PTEN contexts H107 and H108 both clear discovery threshold in favorable signed direction (+0.255 lower +0.165 and +0.261 lower +0.172). H107 active, H108 accepted but deferred due overlap. H80 remains preferred independent validation target because broadest pre-specified PTEN context and largest exposed cell (n=212, lower +0.169). Validate H80 now. If H80 validation lower exceeds 0.15, report PTEN loss as robust conditional association in TP53-loss-free supplied data; if not, report PTEN as reproducible but context-limited/near-threshold, with clean-context H95 and refined contexts as supporting evidence. CDKN2A TP53-loss-free context H109 fails threshold (+0.125 lower +0.051), so close further CDKN2A follow-up; overall H92 remains near-threshold unresolved but inactive. Driver screens: reject/close BRAF H57, ERBB2 H59, MSI-high positive H60; defer unresolved EGFR H58; accept MSI-high negative H106 strongly (+0.792 lower +0.676) as new main supplied-dataset association and keep active for possible later validation/context testing. Registered one follow-up proposal testing MSI-high in TP53-loss-free and KEAP1-loss-free context to ask whether MSI-high remains after removing the two dominant positive architecture effects. Constructed signature_c screens show no loss of association in either half: TP53 low/high +0.391/+0.455 and KEAP1 low/high +0.816/+0.849, all threshold-clearing; interpret only as dataset heterogeneity. Hypoxia interaction for KEAP1 fails and closes biological pathway robustness line. Current core accepted architecture: TP53-loss positive/less-negative, KEAP1-loss positive/less-negative, SMARCA4-loss negative/more-negative, MSI-high negative/stronger-dependency; PTEN conditional/borderline. Continue distinguishing supplied-dataset associations from causal/generalizable claims."
